concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-test-review-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-22b-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "22B(5) Special residence requirement—persons engaged in particular"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-22b-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(g), the Minister may treat a period as one in which the person was not present in Australia as an unlawful non-citizen if the Minister considers the person was present in Australia during that period but, because of an administrative error, was an unlawful non-citizen during that period.  Schedule 2  Amendments relating to special residence requirement" ;
    skos:definition "(5) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(g), the Minister may treat a period as one in which the person was not present in Australia as an unlawful non-citizen if the Minister considers the person was present in Australia during that period but, because of an administrative error, was an unlawful non-citizen during that period.  Schedule 2  Amendments relating to special residence requirement"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "51c4486ed376270a4562d986ef730bf2e076adc81af50a6dbde85762de8e9209" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-test-review-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-22b ;
    cof:pageNumber "12"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "May treat a period as an unlawful non-citizen if administrative error occurred" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
